  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2306.11698",
  "abstract": "This paper presents a comprehensive evaluation of the trustworthiness of GPT models, including GPT-3.5 and GPT-4, from multiple perspectives such as toxicity, stereotype bias, adversarial robustness, out-of-distribution robustness, robustness against adversarial demonstrations, privacy, machine ethics, and fairness. The results show that while GPT models have made significant progress in various tasks, they still have limitations and vulnerabilities that need to be addressed to ensure their trustworthiness.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The trustworthiness of GPT models is a crucial aspect of their development and deployment. <strong>Trustworthiness</strong> encompasses various perspectives, including toxicity, stereotype bias, adversarial robustness, and more. This paper aims to provide a comprehensive evaluation of GPT models from these perspectives, highlighting their strengths and weaknesses.",
